Why this approach: capture hooks 001's existing seams (Rewrite, the response writer, Meta.Settle), so nothing new sits on the byte path beyond two copy-through tees; the queue, store, decoder and parser live outside core.
Alternatives rejected: ncruces/go-sqlite3 (own Go VFS, per-connection Wasm sandbox) and mattn/go-sqlite3 (cgo) for modernc.org/sqlite; cgo zstd and brotli bindings for klauspost/compress and andybalholm/brotli.
Trade-off / known limit: worker memory (joined, decoded bodies) sits outside capture.memory_limit (Q7). Deviations: a Dockerfile change for volume ownership; an unresolvable default capture.dir fails with invalid value.
Verified by: every AC mapped to a test or manual check; AC32-AC36, AC50, AC25 db_deleted and AC57 wait on Q8, Q10 and Q9. Driver facts checked against the ncruces/go-sqlite3 README and pkg.go.dev/modernc.org/sqlite on 2026-09-28.
